SOUTH WIND AROUND 15 MPH.
STRONG WIND THROUGH TUESDAY MORNING.
PORTIONS OFSOUTHWEST GEORGIA AND ALL OF THE EASTERN FLORIDA PANHANDLE =
ANDFLORIDA BIG BEND AWAY FROM THE COAST FOR EARLY MONDAY MORNING. AN =
ARCTIC COLD FRONT WILL MOVE THROUGH THE AREA LATE MONDAYAFTERNOON =
FOLLOWED BY POSSIBLE RECORD BREAKING COLD MONDAY NIGHTINTO TUESDAY. =
ADDITIONAL SNOWFALL AMOUNTS FROM THISNEW STORM HAS THE POTENTIAL TO ADD =
ANOTHER 6 TO 8 INCHES BEFORETHE SNOW MIXES WITH OR CHANGES TO RAIN ON =
TUESDAY. IF YOU OR A PERSON YOU SUSPECT ISSUFFERING FROM FROSTBITE OR =
HYPOTHERMIA. THE WIND CHILL ADVISORY IS NOW IN EFFECT FROM MIDNIGHT =
TONIGHT TO12 PM AST TUESDAY NORTH OF TALKEETNA. NORTHEAST WINDS 15 TO 25 =
MPH WITH GUSTS TO 55 MPH DEVELOPINGOUT OF INTERIOR PASSES THIS EVENING. =
THIS WILL ALLOW FORTEMPERATURES TO DROP BELOW FREEZING IN MANY LOCATIONS =
AWAY FROMTHE COAST FOR 2 TO 4 HOURS BEFORE AND JUST AFTER SUNRISE =
MONDAYMORNING AWAY FROM THE COAST.
ESPECIALLYFOR HIGH PROFILE VEHICLES.
LATE SEASON ARCTIC BLAST TO ARRIVE MONDAY NIGHT. IT WILL FEEL EVEN MORE =
WINTER-LIKE THOUGH AS A CLIPPER LOW DROPSSOUTHEAST FROM THE GREAT LAKES =
AND OFF THE MIDDLE ATLANTICCOAST.
THE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE IN FAIRBANKS HAS ISSUED A WIND =
CHILLADVISORY.
MAKE SURE THAT YOUR PETS ARE ALSO PROTECTEDFROM THE EXTREME COLD. THESE =
STRONG WINDS COMBINED WITH BITTERLY COLD TEMPERATURES WILLPRODUCE WIND =
CHILL VALUES FIVE TO TEN DEGREES DEGREES BELOWZERO.
WE WILL MONITOR THE SITUATION CAREFULLY THAT THE SNOWCOULD POSSIBLY MIX =
WITH OR CHANGE FREEZING RAIN LATE TUESDAYAFTERNOON OR EVENING.
BELOW FREEZINGAIR MAY REMAIN TRAPPED IN SOME LOCATIONS TONIGHT AS =
PRECIPITATIONCHANGES TO RAIN FROM SOUTH TO NORTH.
A STRONG STORM SYSTEM IS EXPECTED TO REMAIN OVER THEGULF THROUGH THE =
REST OF THE WEEK.
IT WILL FEEL EVEN MORE WINTER-LIKE THOUGH AS A CLIPPER LOW =
DROPSSOUTHEAST FROM THE GREAT LAKES AND OFF THE MIDDLE ATLANTICCOAST. =
WITH WIND CHILLS APPROACHING 15 BELOW POSSIBLE ACROSS THEINTERIOR LOWER =
HUDSON VALLEY AND INTERIOR PORTIONS OF SOUTHEASTERNCONNECTICUT. =
ADDITIONAL SNOWFALL AMOUNTS FROM THIS NEWSTORM COULD RANGE FROM ONE TO =
TWO AND HALF FEET.
